  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SUSTAINABLE ENERGY FOR THE HUMANITARIAN HUBS IN NORTHEAST NIGERIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Organization for Migration (IOM) operates eight humanitarian hubs in the Northeast region of Nigeria, serving as the primary provider of such interagency common services in the humanitarian sector. These hubs have played a vital role in delivering lifesaving assistance to four million people in need in Borno state. They not only improve access to affected populations but also enhance coordination, collaboration, and effectiveness among humanitarian responders. The services provided, including secure accommodations, office space, internet access, and meeting/training facilities which enable international and national humanitarian organizations to work effectively in challenging conditions.</narrative>
  </description>
